on homes that have the space for traditional ductwork. It offers even, whole-house cooling and works seamlessly with standard air filtration systems.\n","title_typography_typography":"custom","title_typography_font_family":"Ruda","title_typography_font_weight":"bold","_padding":{"unit":"px","top":"20","right":"20","bottom":"20","left":"20","isLinked":true},"_background_background":"classic","_background_color":"#EDF4FF","_border_radius":{"unit":"px","top":"12","right":"12","bottom":"12","left":"12","isLinked":true},"__globals__":{"primary_color":"globals\/colors?id=accent","title_color":"globals\/colors?id=408e485","hover_title_color":"globals\/colors?id=408e485"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"icon-box","elType":"widget"},{"id":"40e6dec","settings":{"selected_icon":{"value":"spectrelucide- spectre-lucide-heater","library":"spectre-lucide"},"title_text":"Energy-Saving Heat Pumps","description_text":"Don't let the name fool you\u2014heat pumps do an incredible job cooling your home in July. When winter rolls around, they simply reverse the process to keep you warm. They are incredibly popular across North Carolina because they keep electric bills low all year long.\n","title_typography_typography":"custom","title_typography_font_family":"Ruda","title_typography_font_weight":"bold","_padding":{"unit":"px","top":"20","right":"20","bottom":"20","left":"20","isLinked":true},"_background_background":"classic","_background_color":"#EDF4FF","_border_radius":{"unit":"px","top":"12","right":"12","bottom":"12","left":"12","isLinked":true},"__globals__":{"primary_color":"globals\/colors?id=accent","title_color":"globals\/colors?id=408e485","hover_title_color":"globals\/colors?id=408e485"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"icon-box","elType":"widget"},{"id":"780f62ed","settings":{"selected_icon":{"value":"spectrelucide- spectre-lucide-wind","library":"spectre-lucide"},"title_text":"Ductless Mini-Splits","description_text":"Perfect if you are building an addition, converting a garage, or upgrading an older home without space for ductwork. These small, wall-mounted units handle the heating and cooling for individual rooms independently. \n","title_typography_typography":"custom","title_typography_font_family":"Ruda","title_typography_font_weight":"bold","_padding":{"unit":"px","top":"20","right":"20","bottom":"20","left":"20","isLinked":true},"_background_background":"classic","_background_color":"#EDF4FF","_border_radius":{"unit":"px","top":"12","right":"12","bottom":"12","left":"12","isLinked":true},"__globals__":{"primary_color":"globals\/colors?id=accent","title_color":"globals\/colors?id=408e485","hover_title_color":"globals\/colors?id=408e485"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"icon-box","elType":"widget"},{"id":"3d25446a","settings":{"selected_icon":{"value":"spectrelucide- spectre-lucide-gauge","library":"spectre-lucide"},"title_text":"High-Efficiency AC Systems","description_text":"If you want the lowest utility bills possible, these high-performance systems use special variable-speed technology. They automatically adjust their power levels to run on less electricity while keeping your indoor humidity perfectly controlled.\n","title_typography_typography":"custom","title_typography_font_family":"Ruda","title_typography_font_weight":"bold","_padding":{"unit":"px","top":"20","right":"20","bottom":"20","left":"20","isLinked":true},"_background_background":"classic","_background_color":"#EDF4FF","_border_radius":{"unit":"px","top":"12","right":"12","bottom":"12","left":"12","isLinked":true},"__globals__":{"primary_color":"globals\/colors?id=accent","title_color":"globals\/colors?id=408e485","hover_title_color":"globals\/colors?id=408e485"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"icon-box","elType":"widget"}],"isInner":true,"elType":"container"}],"isInner":false,"elType":"container"},{"id":"248ac6df","settings":{"flex_direction":"column"},"elements":[{"id":"327849b9","settings":{"content_width":"full"},"elements":[{"id":"561fa10","settings":{"title":"Our Step-by-Step AC Installation Process\n","align":"center","__globals__":{"title_color":"globals\/colors?id=text"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"66e69cf3","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">A great installation comes down to careful math and neat work. We follow a clear, straightforward process to make sure your new air conditioner works perfectly on day one:<\/span><\/p>","align":"center","__globals__":{"typography_typography":"globals\/typography?id=b279f6f"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"}],"isInner":true,"elType":"container"},{"id":"361ceea7","settings":{"content_width":"full"},"elements":[{"id":"6543cfe2","settings":{"content_width":"full","container_type":"grid","grid_align_items":"start","background_background":"classic","border_radius":{"unit":"px","top":"12","right":"12","bottom":"12","left":"12","isLinked":true},"padding":{"unit":"px","top":"15","right":"15","bottom":"15","left":"15","isLinked":true},"presetTitle":"Grid","presetIcon":"eicon-container-grid","__globals__":{"background_color":"globals\/colors?id=408e485"}},"elements":[{"id":"6bd293e3","settings":{"selected_icon":{"value":"spectrefa- spectre-fa-solid-1","library":"spectre-fontawesome"},"title_text":"Accurate Measurements","description_text":"We calculate your home's exact cooling needs based on its square footage, insulation, and window directions. ","__globals__":{"primary_color":"globals\/colors?id=accent","title_color":"globals\/colors?id=7f92ea2","hover_title_color":"globals\/colors?id=7f92ea2","description_color":"globals\/colors?id=7f92ea2"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"icon-box","elType":"widget"},{"id":"20f0fd7c","settings":{"selected_icon":{"value":"spectrefa- spectre-fa-solid-2","library":"spectre-fontawesome"},"title_text":"Custom Layout Design","description_text":"We map out the shortest, most efficient paths for your indoor air vents. Our goal is to make sure your system pushes air quietly and evenly across every single room.\n","__globals__":{"primary_color":"globals\/colors?id=accent","title_color":"globals\/colors?id=7f92ea2","hover_title_color":"globals\/colors?id=408e485","description_color":"globals\/colors?id=7f92ea2"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"icon-box","elType":"widget"},{"id":"7574889f","settings":{"selected_icon":{"value":"spectrefa- spectre-fa-solid-3","library":"spectre-fontawesome"},"title_text":"Clean Equipment Placement","description_text":"We secure your outside unit on a perfectly flat, durable outdoor pad and set up your indoor equipment with plenty of clear space around it so it is easy to service and clean in the future.\n","__globals__":{"primary_color":"globals\/colors?id=accent","title_color":"globals\/colors?id=7f92ea2","hover_title_color":"globals\/colors?id=408e485","description_color":"globals\/colors?id=7f92ea2"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"icon-box","elType":"widget"},{"id":"1fabb470","settings":{"selected_icon":{"value":"spectrefa- spectre-fa-solid-4","library":"spectre-fontawesome"},"title_text":"Sealing & Pressure Testing","description_text":"We connect the indoor and outdoor parts with copper lines, clear out any hidden moisture, and run a thorough pressure test to guarantee there are absolutely no leaks in the system.\n","__globals__":{"primary_color":"globals\/colors?id=accent","title_color":"globals\/colors?id=7f92ea2","hover_title_color":"globals\/colors?id=408e485","description_color":"globals\/colors?id=7f92ea2"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"icon-box","elType":"widget"},{"id":"60070987","settings":{"selected_icon":{"value":"spectrefa- spectre-fa-solid-5","library":"spectre-fontawesome"},"title_text":"Final Testing & Walkthrough","description_text":"We turn the system on, measure the airflow, and make sure your new thermostat works perfectly. Before we head out, we'll show you how everything operates, explain how to change your filters, and go over your warranty details.\n","__globals__":{"primary_color":"globals\/colors?id=accent","title_color":"globals\/colors?id=7f92ea2","hover_title_color":"globals\/colors?id=408e485","description_color":"globals\/colors?id=7f92ea2"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"icon-box","elType":"widget"}],"isInner":true,"elType":"container"}],"isInner":true,"elType":"container"}],"isInner":false,"elType":"container"},{"id":"5d80a14c","settings":{"flex_direction":"column"},"elements":[{"id":"269552d1","settings":{"width":{"unit":"px","size":200,"sizes":[]},"width_tablet":{"unit":"px","size":"","sizes":[]},"width_mobile":{"unit":"px","size":"","sizes":[]},"align":"center","look":"line_icon","text":"Divider","icon":{"value":"fas fa-check-circle","library":"fa-solid"},"weight":{"unit":"px","size":2,"sizes":[]},"gap":{"unit":"px","size":0,"sizes":[]},"__globals__":{"color":"globals\/colors?id=408e485","primary_color":"globals\/colors?id=accent"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"divider","elType":"widget"}],"isInner":false,"elType":"container"},{"id":"4776c60c","settings":{"flex_direction":"column"},"elements":[{"id":"29840e45","settings":{"content_width":"full"},"elements":[{"id":"1ab9531d","settings":{"title":"Long-Term Benefits of a Professionally Installed AC\n","align":"center","__globals__":{"title_color":"globals\/colors?id=text"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"heading","elType":"widget"},{"id":"6f9b602","settings":{"editor":"<p><span style=\"font-weight: 400;\">Investing in a professionally designed cooling setup completely changes how your home feels:<\/span><\/p>","align":"center","__globals__":{"typography_typography":"globals\/typography?id=b279f6f"}},"elements":[],"isInner":false,"widgetType":"text-editor","elType":"widget"}],"isInner":true,"elType":"container"},{"id":"2a6f9c25","settings":{"content_width":"full"},"elements":[{"id":"5c8c8e4f","settings"